Acceptance criteria:
  Only independently reviewed public-safe source/docs/tracking enter Git.
    No private context, PDFs/reports/captures, browser records or credentials.
  Preserve all four approved README illustration files and references.
    Keep the journal readable, date/provenance honest and actual records untouched.
  Reuse the current workflow; no trigger, permission, secret or scheduler change.
    Verify the exact pushed SHA/run and real hosted result, not an earlier release.
  Retain previous diagnostics and scopes. Source hashes, CI, hosted interactions,
    image inspection and human acceptance are separate evidence.
  Keep the original issue/Project items and Kanban identity; stop conflicting
    edits rather than overwriting them or creating duplicate objects.
  Verify both effective local Git identities and current required trailers for
    each authorized commit. No global attribution/auth changes or history rewrite.
  A documentation-only follow-through must prove runtime/README/workflow/public
    assets identical to the exact deployed source before final handoff.
  Preserve both established previews and all actual browser data. Publication
    approval does not imply personal learning, clinical effect or visual approval.

